course: dictionary
lesson: 16054
title: A good word: virtuous
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Virtuous describes someone who is very good and moral: honest, kind, and doing what is right. «The virtuous knight always helped people in need.» The clue is helped people in need, so virtuous must mean good and kind.
explain: People also use virtuous as a joke. «After eating salad for lunch, Sam felt virtuous.» Sam is not a knight. He is pleased with himself for eating something healthy, so the word is funny here.
explain: A virtuous circle is a chain of good events, where each one causes the next. Its opposite is a vicious circle. When you see a word like circle, look at the words around it to find out what kind of circle it is.
fact: Virtuous means very good and moral, behaving in an honest, kind and right way.
fact: «Virtuous» can also be used humorously, to mean feeling pleased with yourself for doing something good or healthy.
fact: A «virtuous circle» is a chain of good events, each one causing the next.
fact: Virtuous is an adjective. Its forms are virtuous, more virtuous, most virtuous.
fact: Stories, fables and ethics lessons often use virtuous for a good character, the opposite of a wicked one.
exercise: «The virtuous knight always helped people in need.» What does virtuous mean? | *Very good and honest | Very loud | Very tired after a long ride | Very big and strong
exercise: «After eating salad, Sam felt virtuous.» Why does Sam feel virtuous? | *He is pleased with himself for eating something healthy | He is cross because the salad was cold | He is sleepy after lunch | He is lost in the woods
exercise: What is a virtuous circle? | *A chain of good events, each one causing the next | A circle drawn in chalk on the playground | A chain of bad events that keep getting worse | A game where you run in a ring
test: «Her virtuous life made the whole village trust her.» What does virtuous mean here? | *Honest, kind and good | Very quiet | Rich and famous | Lazy and sleepy
test: Which phrase is the opposite of a virtuous circle? | A bright circle of friends | A circle drawn on paper | *A vicious circle | A round table
exam: Tom says, «Mum is virtuous. She gave her seat on the bus to an old man.» What does virtuous mean in Tom's sentence? | Wet through from the rain | Very fast | Lost and confused | *Very good and kind
